  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biodiversity Business in Omo Biosphere Reserve, Oban Biosphere Reserve</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the project is to reduce poverty and contribute to sustainable development and biodiversity in Omo Biosphere Reserve, Oban Biosphere Reserve in Nigeria, and Shere Hills Reserve through the establishment of green economy activities, with a focus on youth and women. Objectives are to - 
 1)	Diversify and improve local economy through improved and alternative green biodiversity related livelihoods.
2)	Build the capacity of communities in a holistic manner to ensure the sustainability of the biodiversity businesses, 
3)	 Enable completion of nomination dossier for Shere Hills Reserve to join the World Network of Biosphere reserve</narrative>
  </description>
